   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi - I just got the attached matrix to work on the Psychotria example, in a non-time-stratified analysis, so match that format.<br><div><br></div><div>File formats: <a href=\"http://phylo.wikidot.com/biogeobears#links_to_files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://phylo.wikidot.com/biogeobears%23links_to_files&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483903966000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2uH_ET56a1O9J-gPrfsnc2\">http://phylo.wikidot.com/biogeobears#links_to_files</a></div><div><br></div><div>But, in general, think carefully about whether the &quot;areas allowed&quot; file is the right approach. It was only designed for a very limited usage:</div><div>==============</div><div>NOTE CAREFULLY: It is impossible to specify all of the possible combinations of allowed/disallowed areas/states that someone might want to do, with just square 1/0 matrices. These are intended for simple cases (like islands sinking as you go back in time).<br><br>You can manually edit the states_list, however, to set up whatever list of allowed states you like. This would be done in the R script and not in a text file. See various discussions on the BioGeoBEARS google group, e.g.<br><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/biogeobears/areas_allowed$20adjacency/biogeobears/7e7U9NtPTBU/pnNtR9M7migJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/biogeobears/areas_allowed$20adjacency/biogeobears/7e7U9NtPTBU/pnNtR9M7migJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483903966000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nnln8vc199bDm-HtD3FeS\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/biogeobears/areas_allowed$20adjacency/biogeobears/7e7U9NtPTBU/pnNtR9M7migJ</a><br></div><div>==============</div><div><br></div><div>See especially:</div><div>Manual modification of states_list (list of geographic ranges, a.k.a. the list of states in the state space)<br></div><div><a href=\"http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts#manual_modify_states\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts%23manual_modify_states&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483903966000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Ajs1W_vKpRTcDT1I9HXuQ\">http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts#manual_modify_states</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Nick</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
